 {
  "id": 36,
  "attributes": {
   "name": "Gas used on transactions",
   "slug": "tezos-chain-gas-used",
   "dataset_key": "tezos-daily-chain-stats",
   "dataset_url": "https://the-stack-report.ams3.digitaloceanspaces.com/datasets/tezos/chain/tezos-daily-chain-stats.csv",
   "x_key": "date",
   "columns": "[\"gas_used_sum\"]",
   "color": "rgb(150,150,150)",
   "description": "Total gas used on transaction operations on the tezos blockchain per day.",
   "rich_description": "Total gas used on transaction operations on the tezos blockchain per day. Gas on Tezos can be thought of as an internal resource that is used up by computations from executing transactions and smart contract code, measured in *gas units* (gu).\n\nThe amount of gas available is limited both per block and per transaction and is set at the protocol level. As can be seen in the chart, these gas limit parameters have been tuned a handful of times already with the various protocol updates.\n\nGas used is **not** measured in _xtz_. But it is one of the inputs in calculating the [minimal fee](https://opentezos.com/tezos-basics/economics-and-rewards/) for a transaction.\n\n---\n\nRelated chart: [Tezos baker fees](/charts/tezos-chain-baker-fee)",
   "type": null,
   "timeline_brush": true,
   "x_type": null,
   "height": null,
   "tooltip_columns_descriptions": null,
   "badges_legend": true,
   "badges_legend_text": null,
   "y_axis_tick_label": "gu",
   "y_scale_type": "linear",
   "createdAt": "2022-09-27T06:02:06.854Z",
   "updatedAt": "2022-09-27T07:25:15.575Z",
   "publishedAt": "2022-09-27T06:02:08.010Z"
  }
 },
 {
  "id": 37,
  "attributes": {
   "name": "Tezos baker fee on transactions",
   "slug": "tezos-chain-baker-fee",
   "dataset_key": "tezos-daily-chain-stats",
   "dataset_url": "https://the-stack-report.ams3.digitaloceanspaces.com/datasets/tezos/chain/tezos-daily-chain-stats.csv",
   "x_key": "date",
   "columns": "[\"baker_fee_xtz_sum\"]",
   "color": "rgb(150,150,150)",
   "description": "Baker fee paid on Tezos transactions per day",
   "rich_description": "Baker fee paid on Tezos transactions per day.\n\nThe primary purpose of transaction fees is to cover the cost of adding a transaction to the blockchain. Tezos bakers can choose to prioritize inclusion of transactions with a higher fee. This implicitly turns _block space_ into an asset sold to the highest bidder (i.e. the agent who includes the highest baker fee in the transaction). \n\nSo far peaks in baker fees mostly come from NFT project launches.",
   "type": null,
   "timeline_brush": true,
   "x_type": null,
   "height": null,
   "tooltip_columns_descriptions": null,
   "badges_legend": true,
   "badges_legend_text": null,
   "y_axis_tick_label": "xtz",
   "y_scale_type": "linear",
   "createdAt": "2022-09-27T06:05:35.406Z",
   "updatedAt": "2022-09-27T07:43:36.245Z",
   "publishedAt": "2022-09-27T06:05:49.556Z"
  }
 },
